'''Sean Berton''' (born October 31, 1979) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[tight end]] in the [[National Football League]] (NFL).  He was undrafted in the [[2003 NFL draft]] after playing [[college football]] for the [[NC State Wolfpack football|NC State Wolfpack]].  The [[Minnesota Vikings]] signed him to a 3-year minimum rookie contract in 2003, but he was released on September 3, 2005.  The [[New York Giants]] claimed him off of waivers where he finished out his rookie contract before being released on May 23, 2006.
